        <Routines>
          <Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Text><![CDATA[MOVE(0,F);]]></Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
          <Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
            <RLLContent>
              <Rung Number="0" Type="N">
                <Comment><![CDATA["Sanity Check" 
Make sure that the sizes  and other config values are correct]]></Comment>
                <Text><![CDATA[[GT(Cfg_NumberOfFaults,64) MOVE(64,Cfg_NumberOfFaults) ,LT(Cfg_NumberOfFaults,0) CLR(Cfg_NumberOfFaults) ,LT(Cfg_CycleTime,0) MUL(Cfg_CycleTime,-1,Cfg_CycleTime) ,LT(Cfg_FaultDurationMin,0) MUL(Cfg_FaultDurationMin,-1,Cfg_FaultDurationMin) ,LT(Cfg_FaultDurationMax,0) MUL(Cfg_FaultDurationMax,-1,Cfg_FaultDurationMax) ];]]></Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="1" Type="N">
                <Comment><![CDATA[Clear the Random number "copy" that is being used in the fault generation - to ensure that the fault is really only triggered once
Copy input Cfg_ data into approrpriate locations]]></Comment>
                <Text><![CDATA[[CLR(RandomNumber) ,MUL(Cfg_CycleTime,1000,TON_Cycle.PRE) MOVE(Cfg_NumberOfFaults,z_CTRL.LEN) SUB(Cfg_NumberOfFaults,1,i_max) ];]]></Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="2" Type="N">
                <Comment><![CDATA[If there are no faults to be generated, there is no need to continue with the code execution]]></Comment>
                <Text><![CDATA[LE(Cfg_NumberOfFaults,0)MOVE(0,F)TND();]]></Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="3" Type="N">
                <Comment><![CDATA[Only generate random number every X milisecond]]></Comment>
                <Text><![CDATA[[XIO(TON_Cycle.DN) TON(TON_Cycle,?,?) ,XIC(TON_Cycle.DN) [AOI_SIM_RNG_Simple(Random) ,MOVE(Random.Number,RandomNumber) ] ];]]></Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="4" Type="N">
                <Comment><![CDATA[Calculate the "fraction" of [0-1] range for each fault = basically the "smallest step" to increment the limit interval
only perform this recalculation once every "fault generation cycle"

1) Sum up all the individual "probability ratios" of all faults
2) check that the "Overall Fault Probability" is within the correct interval
3) calculate the "smallest incrementation step" used for setting comparison limits]]></Comment>
                <Text><![CDATA[XIC(TON_Cycle.DN)[CLR(Wrk_FaultOccurencesSUM) XIO(z_CTRL.DN) FAL(z_CTRL,?,?,ALL,Wrk_FaultOccurencesSUM,Wrk_FaultOccurencesSUM+Cfg_FaultOccurences[z_CTRL.POS]) ,LIMIT(1,Cfg_FaultOccurenceAll,0) MOVE(0.5,Cfg_FaultOccurenceAll) ,NE(Wrk_FaultOccurencesSUM,0) DIV(Cfg_FaultOccurenceAll,Wrk_FaultOccurencesSUM,Wrk_Step) ];]]></Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="5" Type="N">
                <Comment><![CDATA[*********************************************************************************
--> "loop" through the faults
*********************************************************************************]]></Comment>
                <Text><![CDATA[CLR(i)CLR(Wrk_StepLimit1);]]></Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="6" Type="N">
                <Text><![CDATA[LBL(LOOP_Faults)NOP();]]></Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="7" Type="N">
                <Comment><![CDATA[Fault generation

1) compute the comparison limits
2) if the current random number is within the limits, generate the fault]]></Comment>
                <Text><![CDATA[[CPT(Wrk_StepLimit2,Wrk_StepLimit1 + Wrk_Step * Cfg_FaultOccurences[i]) ,GT(RandomNumber,Wrk_StepLimit1) LE(RandomNumber,Wrk_StepLimit2) OTL(F.[i]) ];]]></Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="8" Type="N">
                <Comment><![CDATA[The actual upper limit of the fault's random number will become lower limit in the next cycle of the loop]]></Comment>
                <Text><![CDATA[MOVE(Wrk_StepLimit2,Wrk_StepLimit1);]]></Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="9" Type="N">
                <Comment><![CDATA[When the fault becomes active, set the Preset of the timer to a random value between Cfg_FaultDurationMin seconds and Cfg_FaultDurationMax seconds]]></Comment>
                <Text><![CDATA[XIC(F.[i])ONS(z_ONS[i])[AOI_SIM_RNG_Simple(Random) ,CPT(TONs_FaultHold[i].PRE,(Random.Number * (Cfg_FaultDurationMax - Cfg_FaultDurationMin) + Cfg_FaultDurationMin) * 1000) ];]]></Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="10" Type="N">
                <Comment><![CDATA[When the fault is active, run the timer
And disable the fault when a preset period elapses
]]></Comment>
                <Text><![CDATA[XIC(F.[i])[TON(TONs_FaultHold[i],0,0) ,XIC(TONs_FaultHold[i].DN) OTU(F.[i]) ];]]></Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="11" Type="N">
                <Comment><![CDATA[Next iteration of the loop
or exit]]></Comment>
                <Text><![CDATA[LT(i,i_max)ADD(i,1,i)JMP(LOOP_Faults);]]></Text>
              </Rung>
              <Rung Number="12" Type="N">
                <Comment><![CDATA[Make the last result of Random Number call available to the "outside" (might be useful for some other fault generation procedures)]]></Comment>
                <Text><![CDATA[MOVE(Random.Number,RandomNr);]]></Text>
              </Rung>
            </RLLContent>
          </Routine>
        </Routines>
        <Dependencies>
          <Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="AOI_SIM_RNG_Simple" />
        </Dependencies>
      </AddOnInstructionDefinition>
    </AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
